'  sept: packed text, collection helpers, ordered maps and path trees.
'  .
'  An iota is one path segment: the builtin iota aura-sum.  A path
'  (pith) is a row of iotas: the /path alias.  /uon maps iotas to
'  values, ordered by /lt_iota (size-balanced binary search tree
'  internals, the bst.foil scheme); entries come back in key order.
'  /axal is a tree addressed by paths: each node holds an optional
'  value (fil) and an ordered map of children (kid) — the kid map is
'  /bee specialized to axal child entries.
'  +  each
'    (@@ t)
'    & each/ok[t]
'      each/err
'    + ok
'      : p=t
'    + err
'      : p=pail
'    + map
'      (@ u)
'      \ fun={\ t}u val=each[t]
'      ^ each[u]
'      < (./ok p) val


+  str
